# Nodemailer / SMTP — Gmail.
#   supabase secrets set SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com SMTP_PASS=<app-password>
#
# SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASS are the account the mail is sent FROM. For Gmail
# the password MUST be a 16-character App Password (Google Account →
# Security → 2-Step Verification → App passwords), NOT the account
# password. EMAIL_USER / EMAIL_PASS work as legacy aliases.
#
# Optional — override host/port to use another provider (defaults shown):
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#   SMTP_PORT=465
#
# Optional — overrides the From header. Defaults to SMTP_USER.
#   EMAIL_FROM="HACK2PITCH 2026 <you@gmail.com>"
#
# Heads-up: free-Gmail bulk sends frequently land in the recipient's
# spam folder. A verified custom domain (Resend/SendGrid + SPF/DKIM)
# is the reliable fix if deliverability matters.

# Meta WhatsApp Business Cloud API — the SECOND delivery channel for the
# registration confirmation. SERVER-SIDE ONLY: these are Supabase Edge
# Function secrets, never VITE_ variables and never in the browser.
#   supabase secrets set WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=<system user token> …
#
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN     REQUIRED. System User access token for the
#                           WABA. Treat it like a password: it must
#                           never appear in frontend code, GitHub, logs
#                           or the database. The function never logs it
#                           and redacts it out of Meta error strings.
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID  REQUIRED. Production sender number id.
# WHATSAPP_API_VERSION       Optional. Defaults to 'v23.0' (the Graph
#                           API version this project was tested with).
#
# Optional — override only if the template is ever renamed/re-language:
#   WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NAME=hack2pitch_registration_confirmed
#   WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANGUAGE=en
#
# Optional — country code used ONLY when the lead's stored phone is a
# bare 10-digit national number (the registration form accepts 10–12
# digits, so the country code is not guaranteed to be present).
#   WHATSAPP_DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE=91
# Numbers of any other shape are NEVER guessed: the send is refused with
# LEAD_PHONE_INVALID so the registration can be corrected.
#
# The confirmation reuses the SAME server-generated attendance QR the
# verification email inlines — it is uploaded to Meta's media endpoint
# and referenced as the template's IMAGE header. No second QR is built.
